[h1]Veteran Upgrades[/h1]
Bring the multiplayer veteran upgrade trees into the campaign. Your clan earns points by fighting battles and spends them on upgrades for any unit type - stats, passive traits and battlefield abilities - using the multiplayer skill-tree screen.

Works in all three campaigns: [b]Sengoku Jidai[/b], [b]Rise of the Samurai[/b] and [b]Fall of the Samurai[/b].

[h2]How it works[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Clan points:[/b] your clan earns 1 point for every battle its units fight in, win or lose.
[*][b]Veterans button:[/b] under the advisor button (top left). It lists the unit types your clan can recruit; pick one to open its upgrade tree.
[*][b]Stats:[/b] Melee Attack, Melee Defence, Armour, Morale and Accuracy can each be bought up to 10 times. Every pick costs more than the last, and stronger stats cost more.
[*][b]Abilities:[/b] unlock abilities such as Inspire Unit, Hold Firm, Banzai, Rapid Volley or Increased Range - per unit type, in any combination. Banzai and Blinding Grenades still need their usual research.
[*][b]Upgrades apply clan-wide[/b] to every unit of that type, including ones already in your armies (stats) or newly recruited (abilities).
[*][b]Retrain:[/b] existing units get new abilities by retraining. With an army selected, Retrain swaps that army's units; with nothing selected, Retrain all covers every army. Retrained units appear as a new stack beside the army and lose their experience.
[*][b]Respec:[/b] Reset refunds a unit type's upgrades for a 2-point fee.
[*][b]The AI plays too:[/b] AI clans earn points the same way and buy stat upgrades for the unit types they field.
[/list]

[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Start a new campaign[/b] after enabling the mod.
[*]Recruitment switches to a unit type's new ability set at your next turn. Versions you can't use stay in the recruitment list, greyed out.
[*]Unit names show their abilities, e.g. "Yari Ashigaru (Inspire Unit)" and "Yari Ashigaru (no abilities)".
[*]Ships and generals' bodyguards are not covered.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Veteran Upgrades changes the three campaign scripts (scripting.lua) and the unit-name text. It will conflict with other mods that replace those files. Mods that only change units' stats or add new units are usually fine (new units without a multiplayer equivalent are not upgradeable).

[h2]Source[/h2]
Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/keanfreeman/shogun2-veteran-upgrades]github.com/keanfreeman/shogun2-veteran-upgrades[/url] - bug reports and contributions welcome.
